# TF-901: Fix the return value of Double

## Goal

The function Double in the file math.go of this Go module is intended to return
twice the value of its integer argument, but at the moment it returns a value
that makes the existing unit test in math_test.go fail, so the goal of this task
is to correct the implementation so that the test passes without the test
itself being altered in any way.

## Dependencies

None

## Scope

Edit only the body of the function Double in math.go so that it returns the
argument multiplied by two. Do not rename the function, do not change its
signature and do not modify math_test.go, because the test describes the
required behaviour and has to be treated as the specification.

## Constraints

Do not weaken, delete or edit the test, do not add new dependencies to the
module and do not touch any file other than math.go, and make sure that the
change is committed to the task branch once the checks pass.

## Success criteria

### C1: The unit tests pass

Check: go test ./...

### C2: The test file is unchanged

Check: git diff --quiet main -- math_test.go

## Verification

Run each check from the repository root and report its exit code, and also run
the project wrappers when they exist, reporting the exit code of each.
